<title>BAHRAIN: Saudi Bank al-Jazira Q1 net profit edges higher.</title>
<headline>Saudi Bank al-Jazira Q1 net profit edges higher.</headline>
<dateline>MANAMA 1997-04-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Three months to March 31, 1997</p>
<p>			   (million Saudi riyals)</p>
<p> Net profit		 3.9    vs     3.8</p>
<p> Operating income	58.5    vs    59.7</p>
<p> Expenses		  55.0    vs    55.9</p>
<p> Operating profit	 3.5    vs     3.8</p>
<p> Other income	     0.41   vs     0.04</p>
<p> Shareholders' equity 525.3    vs   511.2</p>
<p> Assets		 3,969.1    vs 4,136.8</p>
<p>Full Name: Bank al-Jazira.</p>
<p>Note - The Jeddah-based bank, traded on the Saudi stock market, is 5.83 percent owned by National Bank of Pakistan. Saudi investors hold the rest.</p>
</text>
